WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.919
- [Reporter:] Oh, God. Oh, no. Make sure you're filming this.

00:00:02.919 --> 00:00:05.296
- Those fools! They couldn't handle it.

00:00:05.296 --> 00:00:08.049
- I was gone 11 days, and the media didn't know what to do.

00:00:08.049 --> 00:00:13.805
- Look, our bad, bro. There was just, like, a lot of attention this offseason.

00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:16.016
- So, yeah, we started a Hype House!

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:19.936
- [Josh Allen:] Whaaaat!
- Yo, bro, what a glow-up.

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:22.564
- [Reporter 1:] He could be MVP.
- [Reporter 2:] He could be MVP.
- [Reporter 1:] He could be MVP
- [Reporter 2:] He could be MVP.

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:23.231
[Doorbell ringing]

00:00:23.231 --> 00:00:25.191
- Cowboys here for our usual hype.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:30.155
- Oh, sorry, my elder dudes. But, like, are you really still going for it in Year 7?

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:36.369
- The 2022 Gridiron Heights Hype House
was the place to be.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.996
You had the Rams…

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:39.789
...the Chiefs...
- [Sighing loudly]

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:42.792
- [Stephen A. Smith] ...And you had Kyle Pitts specifically
 but no one else on the Falcons.

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:45.545
- Uh, hi, I'm Kyle. Is there anything you want me to do
around the house? I can cook, I can—

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.505
- The Hype House was classic media.

00:00:47.505 --> 00:00:53.511
And not the good kind of media where you talk uncontested to a podcaster
in a tank top but the bad kind where they hurt your feelings.

00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:55.138
- Do you even know what TikTok is?

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:57.891
- My favorite show is church.
- Mine too!

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.518
- You let Trey Lance in? But he's barely played!

00:01:00.518 --> 00:01:02.520
- Hey, kid, think you'll have a breakout year?

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.606
[Papers shuffling, whispering]

00:01:04.606 --> 00:01:06.149
- Trey Lance says "yes."

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:07.400
- Who's paying for all of this?

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.651
- Sponsors!

00:01:08.651 --> 00:01:11.696
- And then they made a gargantuan mistake.

00:01:11.696 --> 00:01:14.949
They started hyping up an NFC East team.

00:01:14.949 --> 00:01:18.328
- [TikTok robot voice:] That feeling when people are high
on the Eagles for some reason.

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:23.500
- Hi, I'm a bearded fantasy podcaster, and, look, we were just hyping anybody. Pretty sure I made up Breece Hall.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.506
- Javonte, it's Russ! Man, this is ridiculous. I dressed up for this. I wore my own jersey!

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:34.594
- But as you learn playing for the Bills, some things are just
out of your control, and life's not fair.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.680
- [Producer:] Do you think there's any one person
to blame for what happened?

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.015
- Tyreek, for sure.

00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:40.433
- Yeah, I said what I said.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.602
Yo, everyone, listen.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.853
- Wait, Tyreek, don't.

00:01:43.853 --> 00:01:47.941
- Tua is like if Mahomes and Brady had a baby raised by a JUGS machine.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:54.030
- As I've learned very occasionally in my career, there's some things you just can't say.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:58.827
- So, what happened was the literal weight of expectations got too heavy.

00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:00.662
- Broncos Country...

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:02.247
...I tried.

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:10.130
-[Whispering.]
-Trey Lance says the game has really slowed down for him and credits the coaching staff for his development.

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:14.217
-[Whispering.]
-Trey Lance says he actually likes Jimmy staying and breathing down his neck.

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:20.723
-[Whispering.]
-Trey Lance also says the Falcons Super Bowl loss was a personnel failure and not related to play calling in any way.

00:02:20.723 --> 00:02:23.434
- Tell your friends at home that Geno does deliver!

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:25.854
- So what I like to do is I gel and then blow dry.

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:27.730
- Ooh.
- Oh, interesting.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:31.568
- Hey, bet, say less fellow young coaches.
Uh, hey, Kliff, where's Kyler?

00:02:31.568 --> 00:02:32.652
- Uhhh…

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.363
- See, I prefer to play this game
because it's harder to intercept the grenade.

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:37.407
Oh, wait. I gotta go.

00:02:37.407 --> 00:02:39.492
Take my playbook, not my console!

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.161
Damn, fam, Imma be late as hell.

00:02:43.955 --> 00:02:48.001
Football and gaming combined together…
Ugh, this is like homework.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.586
Oh, hell, yeah, a power-up.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.713
Oh, not cool, fam.

00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:53.464
Uh oh, it's the Fighting Brothers game.

00:02:53.464 --> 00:02:56.718
- You know, I'm sick of our parents
wearing half your jersey and half mine.

00:02:56.718 --> 00:02:58.761
- [All:] There can only be one brother!

00:02:58.761 --> 00:03:02.098
- Go left, Mac-Man...go, uh, right Mac-Man! Uh, right!

00:03:02.098 --> 00:03:03.349
- Oh, Coach is gonna be hella mad.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.060
- First DeAndre, now Kyler. Whatever are we going to do?

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.521
- Everyone, calm down. I coached Mahomes in college.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:09.981
- Phew, that's right.

00:03:09.981 --> 00:03:12.400
- Browns, you piece of s--t gang.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.738
Stop kicking me! Ow. Why are the Browns the one f--king team to make a kick this weekend? Ow!

00:03:16.738 --> 00:03:18.907
- Please let me out. I'll limit my screen time!

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:21.117
- Yeah, of course I tried blowing on it. See?

00:03:21.117 --> 00:03:22.035
 - I'm back, fam.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.745
- You, uh, missed the Chiefs game.

00:03:26.331 --> 00:03:29.959
-Oh, look at my boys, Super Bowl Seany for real for real.

00:03:30.084 --> 00:03:32.503
Rare Seahawks dub, smh.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.465
Tbh, Russ is kinda mid. So I stay ghostin'.

00:03:35.632 --> 00:03:39.928
Yo, Rashaad Penny hits different this year. Sheeesh.

00:03:40.094 --> 00:03:43.806
Yo, I deadass do not know what went down at USC. For real for real.

00:03:43.806 --> 00:03:44.933
- Davante!

00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:46.935
- Aaron?
- Shhh. Listen.

00:03:46.935 --> 00:03:50.063
- "Today on Rogan, we're gonna talk
about spiders: Should you eat 'em?"

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:53.399
- Please come back. You complet...ions me.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.567
- Is everything OK?

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.819
- Go back to bed. We can't be losing sleep, too.

00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:58.446
- Does he take you to big games?

00:03:58.446 --> 00:03:59.739
- He takes up less cap space.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:07.538
- [Voiceover:] After a bad breakup, can this
perennial bachelor find a real catch?

00:04:07.538 --> 00:04:11.876
- The trick is just to find a generational talent and then bury all the
annoying parts of your personality.

00:04:11.876 --> 00:04:14.254
- Kirk, drive me around.
- I'll try.

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:15.213
- [Voiceover:] The heart only gives…

00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:17.632
- Blast them sides, Rodgers.
You look great!

00:04:17.632 --> 00:04:19.425
- [Voiceover:] What it can receive.

00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:22.303
- Wrong route, you stupid a—

00:04:22.303 --> 00:04:23.471
- [Voiceover:] With Aaron Rodgers…

00:04:23.471 --> 00:04:25.014
- What's your favorite part about the Pro Bowl?

00:04:25.014 --> 00:04:27.433
- [Voiceover:] And, uh, Allen Lazard and some guys?

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.352
- Never been.
- I'm Sammy Watkins.
- I dunno.

00:04:29.352 --> 00:04:30.478
- [Voiceover:] This fall…

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:34.732
- Look, things change. I used to be a punter,
and now I'm a media darling. You need to be open.

00:04:34.732 --> 00:04:36.276
- They need to be open!

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:37.944
- [Voiceover:] Some missed connections…

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:39.529
- [Together:] Why do you even want us back?

00:04:39.529 --> 00:04:41.281
- So I can throw to ya any time I want.

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:44.075
- [Voiceover:] Will make you wish you ran for it.

00:04:44.075 --> 00:04:45.868
- Goddamn it, guys! Keep your eyes open!

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.829
- [Voiceover:] Forgetting Davante Adams.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:55.878
-I'm just a quarterback standing in front of a receiver asking him to take a paycut for my sake.

00:04:55.878 --> 00:05:03.094
And most of all, I hate the way these new guys don't catch the ball. Not even a little bit, not even at all.

00:05:03.177 --> 00:05:07.056
I wish I knew how to quit you...and the Packers.

00:05:07.056 --> 00:05:10.935
Nah, just the Packers. I mean, Jerry's been begging me to join the Cowboys.

00:05:10.935 --> 00:05:15.064
- All right, I've got a weak offensive line, no depth on defense
and a new coach who says he knows Aaron Rodgers.

00:05:15.064 --> 00:05:16.149
-That's not what I ordered.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.317
- I thought you could cook anything.

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:21.696
- Guy thinks he can turn The Bronco around, but I heard he flamed out in the big time: Seattle.

00:05:21.696 --> 00:05:24.324
- Behind! We are behind!

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:25.533
Chef, hows the au jeudy?

00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:26.909
- It's simmering?

00:05:26.909 --> 00:05:28.703
- Thank you, Chef. Corner!

00:05:28.703 --> 00:05:33.666
- Yes? You know, Russ, you might get further with people if you stopped acting so...extra all the time.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:34.542
- Heard, Chef.

00:05:34.542 --> 00:05:36.919
- Hey man, uh, look we made another mistake in the bread zone.

00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:40.131
- What's up, Da Bronco?
- Ugh, this guy.

00:05:40.131 --> 00:05:43.009
- Calm down, service isn't for another two hours.

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.386
- Two minutes, Coach. People are already lined up.

00:05:45.386 --> 00:05:47.055
- 10, 9, 8...

00:05:47.055 --> 00:05:55.688
- Third round, 5-foot NUTHIN. You got your bubble water and your fancy headphones. Why are you in charge of the restaurant? I should have let Marshawn run it.

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.065
- Fire! Fire everything!

00:05:57.065 --> 00:05:58.649
- Fired? Already?

00:05:58.649 --> 00:06:01.569
- Remember, separation comes from preparation.

00:06:01.569 --> 00:06:02.779
- Whatever you say, Chef.
- Whatever you need, Chef.

00:06:02.779 --> 00:06:04.572
- I want all the beef.

00:06:04.572 --> 00:06:06.532
- The new special looks like it could be really good.

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:08.534
- Sorry, that's out for like 4-6 months.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.411
- Looks like you're sticking with the usual.

00:06:10.411 --> 00:06:12.038
- Done, Chef.
- That's it?

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:14.499
- Well, we couldn't finish it all so I settled for three.
[bell dings]

00:06:17.168 --> 00:06:20.713
-How are you gonna make a Bear parody and not make it about the Bears?

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:23.299
We're also miserable people trying to make it work in Chicago.

00:06:23.299 --> 00:06:26.427
Smh, I hate this more than I hate the fans.

00:06:26.427 --> 00:06:27.929
I mean...

00:06:27.929 --> 00:06:32.517
- Ja'Marr Chase, Jaylen Waddle, DeVonta Smith. I'll remember
everyone who's in front of me.

00:06:32.517 --> 00:06:35.061
- Bro, we're in a line. It's the Quarter-Season Carnival.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:36.521
- Men, are you ready to play?!

00:06:36.521 --> 00:06:38.272
- Uh, coach? That's the funnel cake stand.

00:06:38.272 --> 00:06:40.775
- Don't matter, everywhere I go I compete.

00:06:40.775 --> 00:06:42.777
- I'll take the biggest prize ever.

00:06:42.777 --> 00:06:46.197
- Uhh, looks like you haven't quite earned it yet. Gotta win a few more games.

00:06:46.197 --> 00:06:47.907
- Still? What about him?

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:50.785
- I haven't even won anything, but people keep giving me prizes!

00:06:53.538 --> 00:06:57.625
- No Ball Pitts today. Maybe next week, maybe not. Go ahead, write our obituary. See if I care.

00:06:58.376 --> 00:07:00.670
- Guys, where are you going? It's all patched up. Good as new.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:03.381
- Try your hand at Trubi-skee ball!

00:07:03.381 --> 00:07:04.507
- Are you gonna play?

00:07:04.507 --> 00:07:05.258
- A little.

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:06.175
- My turn!

00:07:06.175 --> 00:07:07.385
- Why do you still have a baby voice?

00:07:07.385 --> 00:07:09.387
- Last year didn't count.

00:07:09.387 --> 00:07:13.141
- Not yet.
- What? But that creep on the Browns gets rewarded?

00:07:13.141 --> 00:07:15.184
- Hahahaha. Ahahahaha.

00:07:15.184 --> 00:07:16.269
- F--k that elf.

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:17.770
- Just gotta hold 'em off now.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:20.773
- I'm Jalen Hurts. You can like me and still hate Philadelphia.

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:22.316
- Naaah, I need to see more.

00:07:22.316 --> 00:07:25.570
- This year there's a lot of pressure, but it's because everyone believes in me!

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.697
- I can hang. Ah, where's our defense?

00:07:27.697 --> 00:07:29.282
What can I get for all these?

00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:31.784
- Something quite special.
[sad music]

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:34.162
- They just never give us running backs what we deserve.

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:38.416
-You wanna split one or do you want your own?

00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:40.751
-Ahahah, ahahaha.

00:07:40.751 --> 00:07:42.670
-I don't know what that means but I love this kid's motor.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:46.883
-Hahahahaha.
-Oh, yeah, he's got that dog in him.

00:07:46.883 --> 00:07:48.718
- Danny, what did you do?!

00:07:48.718 --> 00:07:51.387
- Oh, God, they think we're killin' it.

00:07:51.387 --> 00:07:52.096
- We're not contenders.

00:07:52.096 --> 00:07:54.974
Do they really expect me to figure it all out in one season?

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:56.851
- If you're a contender, you can't live in this building.

00:07:57.894 --> 00:08:00.146
- We're being set up...by someone we know.

00:08:00.146 --> 00:08:02.231
An overly quirky collection of oddballs, losers...

00:08:02.231 --> 00:08:04.233
...and whatever the f--k the Seahawks are.

00:08:04.233 --> 00:08:05.651
Do we really know any of them?

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.278
And why am I podcasting so much?

00:08:07.278 --> 00:08:09.614
- That's sneaky interesting. Coming up next on the Bill Sim—

00:08:09.614 --> 00:08:12.742
- With our schedule, we've just been taking out the garbage.

00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:14.494
- I already spoke to the authorities. We didn't do anything wrong.

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:19.457
- Sounds like someone spread a nasty little rumor about me...again.

00:08:19.457 --> 00:08:22.877
- They had to be close to us...someone in our division.

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:25.963
- Hey, sorry, still here. Do you guys know how to get ahh!

00:08:25.963 --> 00:08:28.090
- So it's either the Cowboys or the Eagles.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:30.593
- It was me! We're contenders!

00:08:30.593 --> 00:08:32.637
- He's an old man. He doesn't know what he's saying!

00:08:32.637 --> 00:08:34.764
- I'm just humble Jalen Hurts, man.

00:08:34.764 --> 00:08:37.141
- Are you? Just think about it.

00:08:37.141 --> 00:08:39.268
Jalen...Hurts!

00:08:39.268 --> 00:08:41.103
- Oh!
- It's in his name.

00:08:41.103 --> 00:08:42.480
- Hurts people hurt people.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.982
- Fine! Sure, I hid it in college.

00:08:44.982 --> 00:08:48.110
But the truth is, I'm a stone-cold killer!

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:48.986
Arrest me.

00:08:48.986 --> 00:08:51.489
- What? What, no, man. You just have to go live with the good teams.

00:08:51.489 --> 00:08:53.407
- It's been too long. Let's catch up!

00:08:55.993 --> 00:08:59.038
-Comin' up, we'll talk to my buddy Doink about whether the Giants...

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:01.123
...would be better off with a Back like Rex Burkhead.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.208
I'm telling you:

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:05.503
Celery is the nobody-believes-in-us vegetable of crudités.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:08.631
Brian Hoyer: Ewing Theory candidate?

00:09:08.798 --> 00:09:12.635
Is Shaggy from Scooby-Doo the Cordarrelle Patterson of Hanna-Barbera?

00:09:12.635 --> 00:09:16.264
- [Narrator:] Eight months after winning the title,
the Rams are nowhere to be found.

00:09:16.264 --> 00:09:17.974
And now, Carrie Underwood.

00:09:17.974 --> 00:09:21.477
- ♪♪♪ Waitin' all night for morning time. ♪♪♪

00:09:21.477 --> 00:09:23.479
- Oh, what happened?

00:09:23.479 --> 00:09:26.691
- I went into the bathroom to Zac Yak, and there was a tiger in there.

00:09:26.691 --> 00:09:27.441
- What?!

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:29.402
- It's just Who Dey.
- Look away.

00:09:29.402 --> 00:09:32.530
If you've seen one hangover, you've seen 'em all.

00:09:35.199 --> 00:09:36.909
- Has anyone seen Allen Robinson?

00:09:36.909 --> 00:09:39.287
I think you saved him from bears last night?

00:09:39.287 --> 00:09:42.415
- How long have we been out? And whose records are these?!

00:09:42.415 --> 00:09:45.251
- We need to get back into contention before it's too late.

00:09:46.294 --> 00:09:47.545
- I'll catch up with you later.

00:09:48.504 --> 00:09:49.130
- Found Allen!

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.757
- That's Cooper Kupp. You're looking for a different receiver.

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:53.009
- I have other receivers?

00:09:53.009 --> 00:09:55.761
- How much could possibly happen during one party?

00:09:55.761 --> 00:09:57.138
- [Matthew Stafford:] F--k them pics.

00:09:57.138 --> 00:09:59.932
- You guys lost to something called Cooper Rush?

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:01.142
- You did first.

00:10:01.142 --> 00:10:02.893
- Y'all, I think I know how to fix this.

00:10:05.146 --> 00:10:06.272
I wanna go for two.

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:08.441
- You have 19, Coach.

00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:10.568
- Don't worry, guys. I found a few easy games!

00:10:10.568 --> 00:10:14.196
- Where's the last place anyone would expect to find Allen?

00:10:14.196 --> 00:10:15.531
- What the hell, man?!

00:10:15.531 --> 00:10:17.533
- Is that Allen?
- You piece of—

00:10:20.077 --> 00:10:23.289
-I tend to think of myself as a one-man Zac Pack.

00:10:23.289 --> 00:10:26.667
And then we drafted Burrow, and there were two of us in the Zac Pack.

00:10:26.667 --> 00:10:29.879
Um, and then we lost to y'all, in that big ol' game.

00:10:29.879 --> 00:10:31.672
We were like-
-Stop, coach.

00:10:31.672 --> 00:10:32.590
It's played out.

00:10:47.772 --> 00:10:49.732
- TESTING! CHECK ONE! CHECK TWO! HOT ROUTE!

00:10:49.732 --> 00:10:51.525
This is Matt Ryan.
Is this working?

00:10:51.525 --> 00:10:53.027
- Stop yelling.
- Just turn it around.

00:10:53.736 --> 00:10:57.990
- Well, a few of us have experienced an unusual amount of sacktivity.

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:01.118
So we thought we'd move in together and figure out what's going on.

00:11:04.955 --> 00:11:07.083
- Bedtimes for Danny Dimes.

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:11.337
[Glass tinkling, loud crashing]
- Uhhh! Let's ride.

00:11:11.337 --> 00:11:14.465
- See? Right there. A chandelier clearly falls on Russell Wilson.

00:11:14.465 --> 00:11:17.593
- I would've avoided it, but I've been sleeping injured for weeks.

00:11:17.593 --> 00:11:19.470
- And look at this.

00:11:21.263 --> 00:11:23.391
[Thudding]
- Slammy Dimes!

00:11:23.391 --> 00:11:25.768
- Oh, that's just Coach's game plan.

00:11:26.143 --> 00:11:27.478
- Oh, yeah, that's right, Danny.

00:11:27.478 --> 00:11:29.855
Really just throw your body around all willy-nilly.

00:11:29.855 --> 00:11:32.858
- This is just part of the process.
I'm not even being haunted.

00:11:32.858 --> 00:11:34.110
- Sure about that?
[Door creaking]

00:11:36.487 --> 00:11:39.740
- Here, Devonta Freeman. Let's just run the ball.

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:41.784
What the—AAAAH!

00:11:41.784 --> 00:11:44.328
AAAH! AH! AH! AH! AH! Ah, ah...

00:11:44.328 --> 00:11:47.832
I'm giving myself up! Fine, put Ehlinger in.

00:11:47.832 --> 00:11:50.501
- So you really think we're being haunted by D-men?

00:11:50.501 --> 00:11:51.335
- [Matt Ryan:] Yes! Look.

00:11:51.335 --> 00:11:54.630
- [Justin Fields:] It's clearly the ancient D-man, Matthew Judon.

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:56.507
- I called in some protection.

00:11:56.507 --> 00:11:59.885
- Indeed, I can already feel the presence of the D-men.

00:11:59.885 --> 00:12:01.637
We need to prepare ourselves.

00:12:03.347 --> 00:12:06.517
- Out, D-men! Out, Micah Parsons!

00:12:06.517 --> 00:12:09.895
- By the power of Trent f--king Williams: I expel you!

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:13.357
[Crashing, glass breaking]
- I didn't throw these pics, I swear!

00:12:13.357 --> 00:12:14.400
- [In unison:] IN THE NAME OF ANDREW WHITWORTH...

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:15.985
...JOE THOMAS AND ANTHONY MUÑOZ...

00:12:15.985 --> 00:12:17.862
...LET US SEE THE BLIND SIDE.

00:12:18.487 --> 00:12:20.239
- AH!
- Sup, Trent?

00:12:20.239 --> 00:12:21.907
- Oh, hey, Nick. Y'all are f--ked.

00:12:21.907 --> 00:12:22.867
- What do we do?!

00:12:22.867 --> 00:12:25.953
- If you're being attacked by D-men, you need to move!

00:12:25.953 --> 00:12:27.079
- I don't understand.

00:12:27.079 --> 00:12:29.081
- Like, give up and get out.

00:12:29.081 --> 00:12:31.751
- OK, listening to teammate feedback, and we're staying.

00:12:31.751 --> 00:12:33.753
I refuse to scramble anymore.

00:12:33.753 --> 00:12:37.214
- Oh, no. Oh, no!
It's...I'm sorry, who are you?

00:12:37.214 --> 00:12:40.134
- Alex Highsmith. I'm having a really nice season for the Steelers.

00:12:40.134 --> 00:12:43.137
- You know, our media just doesn't do right by you defensive guys.

00:12:43.137 --> 00:12:44.597
- Right?!
- Oooh!

00:12:44.597 --> 00:12:46.390
- How do I not have a single weapon? Ahh!

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:48.225
- [Russell Wilson:] What was that?

00:12:48.225 --> 00:12:50.728
- I heard nobody believes in me.

00:12:50.728 --> 00:12:54.774
- Why are you attacking me?! You're supposed to go through my manager!

00:12:55.775 --> 00:12:59.236
- Grrr! Now gimme that.
I wanna watch the film on this one.

00:13:01.697 --> 00:13:06.994
- And that's why we must do everything we can to stop the d-men.

00:13:06.994 --> 00:13:09.246
- Oh, so scary.
- Aw, man. I hate the d-men.

00:13:09.246 --> 00:13:11.290
- This season they gotta go.

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:12.500
- Per Gridiron Heights guidelines,

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:14.418
the best team in the league runs the town hall.

00:13:14.418 --> 00:13:16.128
- OK, go ahead, Josh.

00:13:16.128 --> 00:13:17.755
- No, the Eagles have the best record.

00:13:17.755 --> 00:13:18.756
- Really?
- Are you sure?

00:13:18.756 --> 00:13:20.132
- It does feel like we're the best, though, right?

00:13:20.132 --> 00:13:21.300
- Order, order!

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.302
- We're gonna follow my very easy schedule.

00:13:23.302 --> 00:13:25.763
There've been some complaints that this season has been weird...

00:13:25.763 --> 00:13:27.890
Two XFL quarterbacks are starting.

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:29.558
Geno Smith is a star.

00:13:29.558 --> 00:13:32.394
And people are actually enjoying themselves in the New York section!

00:13:32.394 --> 00:13:36.398
- ♪ ♪ ♪  I wanna be a part of it...

00:13:36.398 --> 00:13:40.152
...East Rutherford, New Jersey! ♪♪♪

00:13:40.152 --> 00:13:42.238
- I'll now open the meeting up to concerns.

00:13:42.238 --> 00:13:45.783
- We need a town curfew. I'm thinking, like, 4:30.

00:13:45.783 --> 00:13:48.536
- Wait, I have to wear a helmet after my ride is over?

00:13:48.536 --> 00:13:50.746
- Hey, everyone, recycle your quarterbacks.

00:13:50.746 --> 00:13:52.248
- It's not that f--king hard.

00:13:52.248 --> 00:13:55.000
- I don't like how suddenly we're all waking up with aches and pains...

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.419
...and how we all thought we could outrun Father Time forever,

00:13:57.419 --> 00:14:00.422
but now he draws ever closer with each tick of the game clock.

00:14:00.422 --> 00:14:03.008
- Expand the rushing lanes.

00:14:03.008 --> 00:14:05.636
- I'm not here to make excuses.

00:14:05.636 --> 00:14:07.513
I wrote 'em all down before I got here.

00:14:07.513 --> 00:14:08.806
- OK, unless there's any other—

00:14:08.806 --> 00:14:09.682
[Doors busting open]

00:14:09.682 --> 00:14:12.560
- You all thought you could meet up and kick me out.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.270
Well, I've got all your pets, and I'm gonna—

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:16.897
- This is just a normally scheduled town hall meeting.

00:14:16.897 --> 00:14:19.817
- Oh, well, then I guess I'll just sell these back to you, then.

00:14:22.403 --> 00:14:25.322
- Why should I have to direct traffic? People should just know where to go.

00:14:25.406 --> 00:14:27.700
We shouldn't have to work when it's spooky season.

00:14:27.783 --> 00:14:30.286
If other QBs are better, then why don't they debate me?

00:14:30.411 --> 00:14:32.288
There's just a lot of pressure to be...

00:14:32.288 --> 00:14:34.623
...as awful as the guy who had my position before me.

00:14:34.748 --> 00:14:35.833
And another thing!

00:14:35.833 --> 00:14:39.169
It is f***ing bulls**t that the Rodgers Rate isn't real.

00:14:39.169 --> 00:14:41.547
- Ah, Europe. Home of Florida football.

00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:44.633
Nothing says Munich like the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.

00:14:44.633 --> 00:14:46.635
- [German fan:] It's a famed American
hogskin player!

00:14:46.635 --> 00:14:49.013
- Ugh, this happens everywhere I—

00:14:49.013 --> 00:14:50.931
- Geno Smith!
- It's Eugene Smith!

00:14:50.931 --> 00:14:53.517
- It's all about the team, baby. Isn't that right, Tyler Lockett?

00:14:53.517 --> 00:14:54.768
- You know my name? Wow.

00:14:54.768 --> 00:14:57.021
Russ always said that's what our numbers were for.

00:15:00.149 --> 00:15:01.817
- They should call me Kenneth Dancer.

00:15:02.443 --> 00:15:03.193
- Another.

00:15:03.193 --> 00:15:04.904
- It's OK, Tom.
- Want me to fight 'em?

00:15:04.904 --> 00:15:07.531
- So, get this. I told Geno the route to the biergarten...

00:15:07.531 --> 00:15:09.992
...and he actually followed it.
- Woo!

00:15:10.409 --> 00:15:12.369
- No one beats me at hanging out.

00:15:12.369 --> 00:15:13.871
- [All gasping]
- Carbs!

00:15:13.871 --> 00:15:17.875
- Not a single one of my seven rings is worth more than this pretzel!

00:15:17.875 --> 00:15:19.877
Let's f--king gooo!

00:15:20.419 --> 00:15:23.297
- Don't worry, it's no longer Danger-Russ.

00:15:23.297 --> 00:15:26.258
- He has the best foot, so he is the best footballer.

00:15:26.258 --> 00:15:28.385
- Nah, nah, nah.
- That could not matter less.

00:15:28.385 --> 00:15:29.929
- Ugly Americans.

00:15:29.929 --> 00:15:32.514
- So how do you keep getting better as you get older?

00:15:32.514 --> 00:15:35.643
- The trick is to get the hell away from New Jersey.

00:15:35.643 --> 00:15:37.394
- Hey, look, Gronk!

00:15:37.394 --> 00:15:38.938
- Not every white guy with a beard is Gronk.

00:15:38.938 --> 00:15:40.022
Oh, wait, that is Gronk.

00:15:40.689 --> 00:15:41.398
- Prost!

00:15:41.398 --> 00:15:44.151
- [Broadcaster 1:] And nobody showed up today except for the kickers.

00:15:44.151 --> 00:15:46.278
- [Broadcaster 2:] Three points?! That's so many.

00:15:46.278 --> 00:15:48.030
Field goooooooal!

00:15:50.616 --> 00:15:53.410
- And Mariota with a five yard pass to...

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:56.956
...I don't know, I don't care. To take the lead over the coachless Panthers.

00:15:57.373 --> 00:15:57.998
[sigh]

00:15:58.415 --> 00:16:02.336
Goddammit, I'm Al Michaels, and that used to mean something.

00:16:02.336 --> 00:16:03.128
- That's right, Al.

00:16:03.128 --> 00:16:07.007
Also check out Amazon's Thursday Night Football Basketball Football.

00:16:07.007 --> 00:16:12.221
Finally, basketball players talking over football about basketball and maybe football.

00:16:12.221 --> 00:16:14.682
- [Announcer:] Tonight, Gridiron playoff hopefuls will ask our judges...

00:16:14.682 --> 00:16:17.476
"Are You Buying In?"

00:16:17.476 --> 00:16:19.603
First up: the 2022 Saints.

00:16:19.603 --> 00:16:20.562
- Hey, so you should buy in—

00:16:20.562 --> 00:16:22.439
- I'm sorry, pal.
- It's a no for us.

00:16:22.439 --> 00:16:22.940
- Oh.

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:24.692
- Coach Payton, if you're watching this, take me wherever you—

00:16:27.444 --> 00:16:29.363
- [Announcer:] Next up: His dad founded FedEx...

00:16:29.363 --> 00:16:32.199
...but will his playoff invite get lost in the mail?

00:16:32.199 --> 00:16:37.079
- Pitts' production is way DAHN. Yards? DAHN. Catches? DAHN.

00:16:37.079 --> 00:16:37.454
- We're out.
[Buzzer]

00:16:37.454 --> 00:16:40.457
- We're looking for a partial buy-in on a wild-card valuation.

00:16:40.457 --> 00:16:42.167
- Odell?
- Spin around for me.

00:16:42.918 --> 00:16:44.545
Now, dance. Dance for Odell.

00:16:44.545 --> 00:16:47.089
- You know, a good sauce can cover up a bad taste.

00:16:47.089 --> 00:16:48.966
- Mmm, spicy.

00:16:48.966 --> 00:16:50.426
- I guess?
- I'm, like, half in?

00:16:50.426 --> 00:16:51.927
- There's a second New York team?

00:16:51.927 --> 00:16:55.097
- Hit it! Everyone's laughing with me, right?

00:16:55.097 --> 00:16:57.224
- Ugh, they do have really good numbers.

00:16:57.224 --> 00:16:59.184
- Thank you, but I'm declining the offer.

00:16:59.184 --> 00:17:00.811
- We just said you'll win the AFC South.

00:17:00.811 --> 00:17:02.312
- No one deserves to win that division.

00:17:02.312 --> 00:17:04.732
- We're in the top percent of the fourth quadrant.

00:17:04.732 --> 00:17:09.236
Plus, we just named our new coach: the 2014 AFC finalist banner.

00:17:09.236 --> 00:17:11.113
- A proven winner, Mr. Irsay.

00:17:11.113 --> 00:17:12.197
- It did beat the Raiders.

00:17:12.197 --> 00:17:15.451
- [Announcer:] Coming up next:
"Who Wants to Be a Commanders Owner?"

00:17:15.451 --> 00:17:17.953
- All right, all right, all—
- HOV!

00:17:17.953 --> 00:17:20.122
- It seems this is the easiest way for me to get a new team.

00:17:22.708 --> 00:17:25.002
- Yeah, beg. Beg for me, Jerry Jones.

00:17:25.127 --> 00:17:28.005
Ok, hold on. Wait. How many fashion weeks does Buffalo have?

00:17:28.005 --> 00:17:28.881
None?!

00:17:29.006 --> 00:17:32.593
Rename Jerry World? Odell World.

00:17:32.593 --> 00:17:33.260
Do it, old man!

00:17:35.471 --> 00:17:36.764
You've gotta be f--kin' kidding me.

00:17:36.764 --> 00:17:38.098
All right, pilots, bring it in.

00:17:38.098 --> 00:17:40.517
I've retired from the MVP race of my own accord.

00:17:40.517 --> 00:17:42.019
- Oh, OK.
- So humble.

00:17:42.019 --> 00:17:43.103
- You were clearly forced out.

00:17:43.103 --> 00:17:45.355
- Anyway, I'll be your eye in the sky, and this is your flight path.

00:17:45.355 --> 00:17:46.648
Do you understand?

00:17:46.648 --> 00:17:50.486
- Looks all right to me. Or should I say all left, Tagovailoa?

00:17:50.486 --> 00:17:51.779
[Laughing]

00:17:51.779 --> 00:17:54.531
- Remind me, Hurts, who's the only undefeated pilot left?

00:17:54.531 --> 00:17:55.115
- [Gasping]

00:17:55.115 --> 00:17:57.618
I was ordered to stand down by my superior commanders...

00:17:57.618 --> 00:17:58.744
...and I actually followed protocol.

00:17:58.744 --> 00:18:00.245
[Multiple players gasping]

00:18:00.245 --> 00:18:02.206
- This year, it's an airplane race!

00:18:02.581 --> 00:18:05.250
- [Aaron Rodgers:] Clear for takeoff in 3...2...1.

00:18:09.588 --> 00:18:12.341
- Let's put a little more air under it. I'm not sure we can keep this up.

00:18:12.341 --> 00:18:14.259
- Why does everyone keep saying that to me?

00:18:14.259 --> 00:18:18.013
- An OG plane for me: the original gangster, Kirk Cousins.

00:18:18.013 --> 00:18:20.099
This is so easy!

00:18:22.601 --> 00:18:24.853
[Dinging]
- Oh, no! It's the Jets stream.

00:18:25.395 --> 00:18:27.106
- I'm just mashing buttons!

00:18:27.106 --> 00:18:29.483
- Geno, is that a glider?
- Yes, indeed.

00:18:29.483 --> 00:18:31.235
- You know it can only go so far, right?

00:18:31.235 --> 00:18:33.403
- I knoooow.

00:18:33.403 --> 00:18:34.613
- Coach, we're almost out of fuel.

00:18:36.365 --> 00:18:37.407
Do you receive me?

00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:39.493
Does...does anyone receive me?

00:18:40.494 --> 00:18:41.870
- Where did that come from?!

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:44.957
- Blindside blitz. Goodbye, Frog Man.

00:18:45.999 --> 00:18:49.461
- [Rodgers:] Don't worry, folks.
We have taken out the defender.

00:18:49.461 --> 00:18:52.631
- Joe Cool here. Losing some visibility. Need a read here.

00:18:52.631 --> 00:18:53.632
- One second!

00:18:56.343 --> 00:18:57.594
OK, so there's a mountain coming up.

00:19:00.389 --> 00:19:03.600
- Fly, Eagles, fly!

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:05.227
- Wheeeee!

00:19:05.227 --> 00:19:07.604
- Don't make any stupid mistakes, Josh!

00:19:07.604 --> 00:19:09.398
- Nah, come on. Do something reckless.

00:19:09.398 --> 00:19:10.482
- That sounds fun!

00:19:10.482 --> 00:19:11.775
- Barrel roll it is!

00:19:13.861 --> 00:19:16.488
- [Rodgers:] How is this guy still flyin' under the radar?

00:19:16.488 --> 00:19:18.782
They're approaching the final turn along Press Row.

00:19:18.782 --> 00:19:20.242
And Tua surpasses Hurts!

00:19:20.242 --> 00:19:22.369
- Just like at the academy, woo!

00:19:23.662 --> 00:19:27.249
- ♪♪♪ Shirtless men settling differences through sports! ♪♪♪

00:19:27.249 --> 00:19:29.376
- Not again!

00:19:29.835 --> 00:19:32.212
- [Rodgers:] At that speed, they'll never be able to survive the pressure.

00:19:32.212 --> 00:19:33.881
The J Force is too much.

00:19:33.881 --> 00:19:35.591
- [Reporter 1:] Hurts' flight path was easier.

00:19:35.591 --> 00:19:37.092
- [Reporter 2:] Can Mahomes do it without Tyreek?

00:19:37.092 --> 00:19:38.635
- [Reporter 1:] I still don't think Tua's that good.

00:19:38.635 --> 00:19:40.220
- I can win MVP!

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:41.513
- I have won MVP!

00:19:41.513 --> 00:19:43.348
- I can win MVP!

00:19:43.348 --> 00:19:44.725
- Look out, look out, look out!

00:19:47.102 --> 00:19:49.855
- Let's just avoid any unforced errors.

00:19:49.855 --> 00:19:51.648
- It's like we always say...

00:19:51.648 --> 00:19:55.277
- You can't make an omelet without breaking a few tables.

00:19:55.277 --> 00:19:56.945
- Uh oh, snow.

00:19:56.945 --> 00:19:59.740
- Better move to Detroit for a week. Jinx!

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:03.827
- Ah, jeez. You never get used to seeing a team's chances die, do yah?

00:20:03.827 --> 00:20:05.829
- Kirk, man, why you gotta sound so corny all the time?

00:20:05.829 --> 00:20:07.372
- I'm not dead yet.

00:20:07.372 --> 00:20:10.083
- Ah, you betcha yah are there, guy.

00:20:18.634 --> 00:20:20.802
- So, someone killed the Packers, and all they took was

00:20:20.802 --> 00:20:23.555
a briefcase with the title to the division in it?

00:20:23.555 --> 00:20:26.767
- Can you think of anyone who would have a grudge against Aaron Rodgers?

00:20:26.767 --> 00:20:27.517
- [Together:] Yes.

00:20:27.517 --> 00:20:28.769
- Op, there he is.

00:20:28.769 --> 00:20:29.728
- We got a runner.

00:20:30.479 --> 00:20:31.271
Are you a killer?

00:20:31.271 --> 00:20:32.397
- Not in real life...

00:20:32.397 --> 00:20:34.274
...but in my fantasies.

00:20:34.274 --> 00:20:36.735
- Oh, well. Who could care about that? Goodbye!

00:20:38.237 --> 00:20:40.113
- There's someone sticking out of the woodchipper.

00:20:40.113 --> 00:20:42.741
- Oh, another spectacular catch there, Justin.

00:20:42.741 --> 00:20:45.285
- I was just making some Packer kneecap for dinner.

00:20:45.285 --> 00:20:47.162
By the time we got to them, they were already dead.

00:20:47.162 --> 00:20:48.121
- Why a woodchipper?

00:20:48.121 --> 00:20:48.747
- Because it's hardcore.

00:20:48.747 --> 00:20:49.748
- Wait, stop!

00:20:51.124 --> 00:20:54.378
Oh, sorry, it's getting late. I don't shoot so well when I'm tired, eh.

00:20:54.378 --> 00:20:55.629
Oh, give me a sec.
- Oh!

00:20:56.797 --> 00:20:58.257
- I'm sorry, sir. Who are you?

00:20:58.257 --> 00:21:00.425
- Your coach, Kevin O'Connell.

00:21:01.301 --> 00:21:02.803
You know, one of McVay's little buddies?

00:21:02.803 --> 00:21:04.429
- Ohhh. Hey, Coach.

00:21:04.429 --> 00:21:07.516
So, you're saying we, the humble Midwestern Vikings...

00:21:07.516 --> 00:21:09.476
...have been killers the whole time?

00:21:09.476 --> 00:21:10.978
I just don't understand it.

00:21:10.978 --> 00:21:12.479
Op, just ran over the Pats.

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:16.984
- You like the radio, there, coach?

00:21:16.984 --> 00:21:18.485
- [Radio Announcer 1:] Be advised: the Vikes are on the run...

00:21:18.485 --> 00:21:19.736
...and they do have weapons.

00:21:19.736 --> 00:21:21.238
- [Radio Announcer 2:] Yah, but if I know the Vikes...

00:21:21.238 --> 00:21:22.572
...they never get too far.

00:21:22.572 --> 00:21:25.575
- [Radio Announcer 1:] Hahaha, you're right! So, it's just a matter of time.

00:21:25.575 --> 00:21:27.411
- Op, that's enough of that, there.

00:21:27.411 --> 00:21:28.912
- Welcome to the golden hour!

00:21:28.912 --> 00:21:32.249
Where the ugly look beautiful and the beautiful look like everyone else.

00:21:32.249 --> 00:21:35.294
- It's over for y'all once we finish animating Brock Purdy.

00:21:35.294 --> 00:21:38.797
- Oh, little old me in a photo? Haha.
 Sure, I guess. Haha.

00:21:38.797 --> 00:21:40.424
- Oh, stop it. You're 8-4.

00:21:40.424 --> 00:21:41.425
- Where are the Titans?

00:21:41.425 --> 00:21:43.552
- We're behind Brian's hat.

00:21:43.552 --> 00:21:45.053
- [All affectionately:] Briaaan.

00:21:45.053 --> 00:21:46.305
- Lamar's out for a few snaps.

00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:48.098
Oh, wait! I'm getting a tweet alert!

00:21:48.098 --> 00:21:51.601
STFU y'all be cap—OK, this is very problematic.

00:21:51.601 --> 00:21:52.436
Cut to commercial!

00:21:52.436 --> 00:21:54.479
- [Producer:] We don't do that.
- Make an exception!

00:21:57.024 --> 00:22:00.402
Let's go to a quadbox to check in on all four NFC East teams.

00:22:00.402 --> 00:22:02.779
- YELLING! CHEESESTEAKS! HEART!

00:22:02.779 --> 00:22:05.782
- No, no! Group photos always get me in trouble.

00:22:05.782 --> 00:22:08.201
- That monster on the Browns is back.

00:22:08.201 --> 00:22:09.286
- Ahahahaha.

00:22:09.286 --> 00:22:10.704
- Where's our NFC South rep?

00:22:10.704 --> 00:22:15.667
[Sad violin music]

00:22:15.667 --> 00:22:16.585
[Regal trumpet]

00:22:16.585 --> 00:22:19.171
- Make way for Mike White, the king of New York!

00:22:19.171 --> 00:22:20.422
- Hi! Hello!

00:22:20.422 --> 00:22:21.798
- [Together:] I hate the Jets.

00:22:21.798 --> 00:22:24.176
- Oh, man. Up top Justin Herbert has entered the picture,

00:22:24.176 --> 00:22:26.678
while Geno Smith is also making a move.

00:22:26.678 --> 00:22:29.723
- Sorry I'm late. The breaks have been, like, weirdly bad lately.

00:22:29.723 --> 00:22:31.933
- OK, we're losing light. Smile.

00:22:31.933 --> 00:22:34.102
[Camera shutter]
Well, at least the AFC looks nice.

00:22:36.688 --> 00:22:39.691
- Oh no, where is everyone? What's going on?

00:22:39.691 --> 00:22:41.943
- Calm down, Kirk. It's just nighttime.

00:22:41.943 --> 00:22:44.780
- Prime time, where the Cowboys shine!

00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:47.532
Oh wait, the tide is carrying me away!

00:22:47.532 --> 00:22:48.867
- [all:] Someone grab Jerry!

00:22:48.867 --> 00:22:49.910
[Thumping on roof]

00:22:49.910 --> 00:22:51.078
- [Jimmy Garoppolo:] Another great drive, babes.

00:22:51.912 --> 00:22:53.830
Kittle, babe, you GOTTA condition that long hair.

00:22:53.830 --> 00:22:54.873
We got enough split ends.

00:22:55.707 --> 00:22:56.833
- Whoa, whoa, not again!

00:23:03.131 --> 00:23:05.342
- Nah, that would be too dark for a kids program.

00:23:05.342 --> 00:23:06.718
See you in the postseason, Brick.

00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:09.763
- Woo, it's a physical sport. Next man up.

00:23:09.763 --> 00:23:11.640
- CMC drives sleigh.

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:15.268
This Santa Clause seems like it's on very shaky legal ground, no?

00:23:18.647 --> 00:23:20.732
- You're in charge of distributing the footballs now.

00:23:21.608 --> 00:23:23.860
- We don't like to think about next year here in Santa's Clara.

00:23:23.860 --> 00:23:25.987
- Deebo will help you with anything you need.

00:23:25.987 --> 00:23:28.532
- Oh, great. More things for me to do.

00:23:28.532 --> 00:23:30.117
- And this is Bosa, our Sackmaster.

00:23:30.117 --> 00:23:31.243
- Haha, sack.

00:23:33.787 --> 00:23:37.249
And my voice is deeper? Oh no, is this a horror story?

00:23:37.249 --> 00:23:39.126
- Look, it happens all the time. See?

00:23:39.126 --> 00:23:40.627
- Guess I gotta buy some shoes to fill.

00:23:40.627 --> 00:23:43.130
- Oh, boy. This is a rough game.

00:23:43.130 --> 00:23:45.382
- Don't mind if I f--kin' do.

00:23:45.382 --> 00:23:48.385
- Flac-ho ho ho! Look who's came crawling back?

00:23:48.385 --> 00:23:49.302
- I didn't even get hurt!

00:23:49.886 --> 00:23:51.430
- Keep an eye on the internal clock on the sleigh.

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:53.014
You have three seconds to deliver each ball.

00:23:53.014 --> 00:23:53.765
- Hut, hut.

00:23:53.765 --> 00:23:55.600
- Nothing over five yards, OK, Brock?

00:23:58.186 --> 00:24:01.314
- Jingle bell, jingle bell, jingle bell Brock.

00:24:01.898 --> 00:24:03.608
Jingle around the-

00:24:03.608 --> 00:24:04.484
-Hey.

00:24:04.484 --> 00:24:05.610
- He does exist.

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:06.987
- He does exist.

00:24:08.572 --> 00:24:11.700
- They told me I was a lineman, not a frontman.

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:12.826
- This is our big chance!

00:24:12.826 --> 00:24:14.744
Every single person from the media showed up.

00:24:14.744 --> 00:24:16.580
- I have a major announcement.

00:24:16.580 --> 00:24:18.331
It's the Eagles!
[Audience cheering]

00:24:18.331 --> 00:24:19.249
The football team.

00:24:19.249 --> 00:24:20.083
- [Audience:] Aww.

00:24:20.083 --> 00:24:23.378
- Jingle bells, jingle bells...
[Snickering]

00:24:23.378 --> 00:24:25.714
♪♪♪ Jingle all the way. ♪♪♪
[Cheering]

00:24:25.714 --> 00:24:28.091
- Oh, my God, they're better than the Chiefs!

00:24:28.967 --> 00:24:30.969
- Eaglemania swept the nation.

00:24:30.969 --> 00:24:34.598
And who managed that s--t but me, Nicky Sirianni?

00:24:34.598 --> 00:24:37.184
- I heard you're looking for a little of that Nashville sound.

00:24:37.184 --> 00:24:39.936
- So, crikey, the head 'ranger wanted to add some joeys.

00:24:39.936 --> 00:24:41.813
- He means Sirianni added some folks.

00:24:41.813 --> 00:24:44.858
- Things did get a little weird when the band entered their Batman era.

00:24:44.858 --> 00:24:47.861
- ♪♪♪ Dark Knight,

00:24:47.861 --> 00:24:50.947
Bruce Wayne. ♪♪♪

00:24:50.947 --> 00:24:53.366
- They were the Eagles, but then they added bats.

00:24:53.366 --> 00:24:54.618
It was too many animals.

00:24:54.618 --> 00:24:57.954
- You've changed, Jason. I'm supposed to be the hot brother.

00:24:57.954 --> 00:25:00.207
- ♪♪♪ You're a mean one, Mr. Snyder. ♪♪♪

00:25:00.207 --> 00:25:01.458
[Cheering]

00:25:01.458 --> 00:25:04.211
- We got upstaged by the f--king Commanders.

00:25:06.338 --> 00:25:08.006
- ♪♪♪ Daboll, Daboll, Daboll.

00:25:08.006 --> 00:25:09.466
The refs threw the game our way. ♪♪♪

00:25:09.466 --> 00:25:10.717
- Maybe I could play lead?

00:25:10.717 --> 00:25:11.718
- Quiet, Tony Pollard!

00:25:11.718 --> 00:25:12.886
Zeke's the star.

00:25:12.886 --> 00:25:15.847
- We had to get back to what got us there in the first place.

00:25:15.847 --> 00:25:16.973
- No rules, just right.

00:25:16.973 --> 00:25:18.934
- This one goes out to all the haters.

00:25:18.934 --> 00:25:21.561
♪♪♪ We wish you a Merry Christmas! ♪♪♪

00:25:24.773 --> 00:25:26.775
- [Doug Pederson narrating:]
I washed out of Philly.

00:25:26.775 --> 00:25:29.152
This strange land was my last chance.

00:25:30.403 --> 00:25:31.696
OK, we can work on that release.

00:25:32.531 --> 00:25:34.950
-  [Pederson narrating:] They'd had bad experiences with outsiders.

00:25:34.950 --> 00:25:37.160
- OK, let's make this place look and feel like Ohio.

00:25:37.160 --> 00:25:39.454
- [Pederson narrating:] They spoke in a foreign tongue.

00:25:39.454 --> 00:25:40.664
- Duval!

00:25:40.664 --> 00:25:43.542
- [Pederson narrating:] But they embraced me as their own.

00:25:43.542 --> 00:25:46.670
- Let me show you...the way of the cat teams.

00:25:49.381 --> 00:25:51.132
- Aaaaah.

00:25:51.132 --> 00:25:53.969
- [Pederson narrating:] For the first time in eons, all four clans had a chance.

00:25:53.969 --> 00:25:58.348
- You either die a hero or live long enough to become a Panther.

00:25:58.348 --> 00:25:59.641
- We just gotta attack the Pack.

00:25:59.641 --> 00:26:02.477
- We also need the Seahawks to lose to the Rams.

00:26:02.477 --> 00:26:03.353
- You nerds with your mythology.

00:26:04.729 --> 00:26:07.357
- Why are you all blue? Cats aren't blue.

00:26:07.357 --> 00:26:09.359
- I'm a Zac cat, y'all. Meow.

00:26:09.359 --> 00:26:12.279
- [Pederson narrating:] But the Titans were coming for us.

00:26:12.279 --> 00:26:14.155
- Wait, who's driving this thing?

00:26:14.155 --> 00:26:15.115
[Banging, splashing]

00:26:15.115 --> 00:26:16.074
- Dobbs?

00:26:16.074 --> 00:26:16.908
[Squeaking]

00:26:16.908 --> 00:26:18.910
- We need to think like them.

00:26:18.910 --> 00:26:20.662
- Man, what the hell are you doing with your ponytail?

00:26:20.662 --> 00:26:22.747
- Hold the line! Wait.

00:26:22.747 --> 00:26:23.790
What's in the water?

00:26:24.249 --> 00:26:25.750
[Splashing]

00:26:25.750 --> 00:26:29.254
Oh, God, these special effects are TOO realistic!

00:26:32.924 --> 00:26:36.720
- For years the bird teams have kept the cat teams at bay.

00:26:37.220 --> 00:26:38.972
Must the Eagles clan do everything?

00:26:38.972 --> 00:26:40.473
- Yeah, our bad, fam.

00:26:40.473 --> 00:26:42.058
- Fix. It.

00:26:42.058 --> 00:26:43.768
- Alright. Hey, Coach Kingsbury.

00:26:43.768 --> 00:26:44.519
See that cliff?

00:26:44.519 --> 00:26:47.188
- [Kingsbury:] No, no, no, no. I am Kliff.

00:26:47.188 --> 00:26:48.857
Woaaaaah!

00:26:48.857 --> 00:26:50.859
- [Murray:] Oh, whoops, I pushed you out.

00:26:50.859 --> 00:26:53.194
- Thank God I'm missing the playoffs so I can focus on research.

00:26:53.194 --> 00:26:56.489
- Are you down and out and unsure what to ride into the playoffs?

00:26:56.489 --> 00:26:57.866
At Chargers Auto Group,

00:26:57.866 --> 00:27:01.870
our bandwagon is huge, and this bad boy is very empty.

00:27:01.870 --> 00:27:04.247
- It's all electric, and it comes in dope colors.

00:27:04.247 --> 00:27:05.540
- Not sure about budget?

00:27:05.540 --> 00:27:06.416
- We're flexib—

00:27:06.958 --> 00:27:09.919
- Exceeding expectations with a QB you've talked yourself into:

00:27:09.919 --> 00:27:12.380
the Throwback Giants Bandwagon.

00:27:12.380 --> 00:27:13.882
It can be 2008 again.

00:27:14.257 --> 00:27:16.760
- You name it, we got it! All the bells and whistles.

00:27:16.760 --> 00:27:18.053
- A strong defense!
- Check.

00:27:18.053 --> 00:27:19.471
- A franchise quarterback.
- Well...

00:27:19.846 --> 00:27:22.349
- OK, yeah, our cars are gonna break on ya.

00:27:22.349 --> 00:27:23.475
But that's why we got a...

00:27:23.475 --> 00:27:25.560
[Alarm blaring]
- Next One Up policy. Woo!

00:27:25.560 --> 00:27:28.104
- That's right. We've got seemingly unlimited options.

00:27:28.104 --> 00:27:29.648
So come on down to the Niners.

00:27:29.648 --> 00:27:31.316
- [All:] We'll get there somehow.

00:27:31.691 --> 00:27:34.361
- I've got three words for you: No money down!

00:27:34.361 --> 00:27:35.195
Right, Lamar?

00:27:35.195 --> 00:27:37.280
- I'm not selling s--t until I get my commission!

00:27:37.656 --> 00:27:39.741
- Yo, if you didn't support us from day one, f--k off.

00:27:39.741 --> 00:27:41.660
#NoNewFans. Wagon's not for sale.

00:27:42.035 --> 00:27:45.163
- Yeah, she's got some miles on her, but she's as reliable as always.

00:27:45.163 --> 00:27:46.539
And don't you ever forget that.

00:27:46.790 --> 00:27:49.876
- I really wish you would stop asking about our safety features.

00:27:49.876 --> 00:27:50.251
[Alarm ringing]

00:27:50.752 --> 00:27:52.253
- What's up, sports fans?

00:27:52.253 --> 00:27:53.421
Sure, we're out of it.

00:27:53.421 --> 00:27:56.132
But do you really wanna go with a fancy playoff dealership?

00:27:56.132 --> 00:27:58.093
Or do you wanna watch me lift that sedan?

00:28:02.472 --> 00:28:06.017
- Do not, I repeat do not, come down to Arrowhead Automotive.

00:28:06.017 --> 00:28:08.353
There's no more space on our bandwagon!

00:28:08.353 --> 00:28:10.980
That's right, our bandwagon is full and closed,

00:28:10.980 --> 00:28:12.774
because everyone loves us so much.

00:28:13.483 --> 00:28:14.901
- Thanks for the drive, Zeke.

00:28:14.901 --> 00:28:17.404
- OK, Dak, enter the casino. You just need to win one—

00:28:17.404 --> 00:28:19.531
- OK, tell Dak he just needs to win—

00:28:19.531 --> 00:28:21.783
- OK, tell Kellen Moore to tell Dak to win.

00:28:25.620 --> 00:28:26.746
- [Announcer:] Interception!

00:28:26.746 --> 00:28:29.791
- [Jerry Jones:] Careful, you're surrounded by serious threats.

00:28:29.791 --> 00:28:32.252
- So, uh, my dude. What are the rules?

00:28:32.252 --> 00:28:34.003
- Oh, I thought you had done this before.

00:28:34.003 --> 00:28:34.671
- I call.

00:28:35.422 --> 00:28:36.506
- I ain't call back, though.

00:28:36.506 --> 00:28:38.383
- Wait, I have to play Tom Brady?

00:28:38.383 --> 00:28:40.301
The Bills get to play against Skylar Thompson.

00:28:40.301 --> 00:28:41.761
- Go fish!

00:28:41.761 --> 00:28:44.097
- No, no, no. Go Bills.

00:28:44.097 --> 00:28:45.724
- [Dak:] And I don't even know who is left for Baltimore.

00:28:45.724 --> 00:28:47.892
- You're Ray Lewis with a fake moustache.

00:28:47.892 --> 00:28:49.477
- Man, I said I'm No-Name Johnson.

00:28:49.477 --> 00:28:51.104
And I lettered at Minnesota Southern.

00:28:51.104 --> 00:28:53.898
- OK, daddy needs to recoup massive crypto losses.

00:28:53.898 --> 00:28:56.484
- Looks like Brady's tell is that every time he's inconvenienced,

00:28:56.484 --> 00:28:58.278
he destroys a tablet.

00:28:58.278 --> 00:29:00.530
- Stupid thing givin' me bad cards!

00:29:00.530 --> 00:29:01.531
[Banging and shattering]

00:29:01.531 --> 00:29:02.240
- Call.

00:29:02.240 --> 00:29:05.118
- Ah, once again, bested by my enemy...

00:29:05.118 --> 00:29:05.869
DVOA.

00:29:05.869 --> 00:29:06.911
- How'd I do?

00:29:06.911 --> 00:29:09.247
- Wait, wait.
- [Together:] Is this kid, like, really good?

00:29:09.247 --> 00:29:10.248
- Hey, man...

00:29:10.248 --> 00:29:11.875
- [Together:] I love your hair. Jinx!

00:29:11.875 --> 00:29:13.626
- There, there. You're coming with me.

00:29:13.626 --> 00:29:15.253
- OK, let's see your cards.

00:29:15.253 --> 00:29:16.004
- We won.

00:29:16.004 --> 00:29:18.757
- Please give me some privacy as I publicly mull retirement.

00:29:21.301 --> 00:29:24.304
- Shaken not stirred, what the f**k is that?

00:29:24.304 --> 00:29:26.181
All we have is warm Yuengling and water.

00:29:26.181 --> 00:29:28.641
- Um, I can make you a burger if I can find you a grill.

00:29:28.641 --> 00:29:29.768
Oh, they left.

00:29:30.852 --> 00:29:32.353
- You know, I used to coach the Eagles.

00:29:32.353 --> 00:29:33.855
- Very cool.

00:29:33.855 --> 00:29:35.064
- I'd like to order a private plane.

00:29:35.064 --> 00:29:37.817
Destinations Miami, San Fran, Vegas, Foxb—

00:29:37.817 --> 00:29:38.818
What is that noise?!

00:29:39.569 --> 00:29:41.571
- It's easy money, and you barely have to play.

00:29:41.571 --> 00:29:42.989
- Yeah, but Indianapolis?

00:29:42.989 --> 00:29:44.365
- Beer me, Aaron!
[Crashing and fizzing]

00:29:44.365 --> 00:29:47.619
- Looks like that one hit..."LaFloor." Hahahaha.

00:29:47.619 --> 00:29:49.329
- Why is your body making those noises?

00:29:49.329 --> 00:29:50.705
- I'm doing a laughing, Tom.

00:29:50.705 --> 00:29:52.749
I'm happy! Turns out during the playoffs,

00:29:52.749 --> 00:29:55.460
everyone else stays in Gridiron Heights and gets along.

00:29:55.460 --> 00:29:56.461
Have a cold one.

00:29:56.461 --> 00:29:58.963
- Why? To be relatable on late-night TV?

00:29:58.963 --> 00:30:01.216
- Everyone's welcome. Isn't that right, Russ?

00:30:01.216 --> 00:30:02.342
We also got catering.

00:30:02.342 --> 00:30:05.428
- The Jets are happy to sponsor the offseason dance contest...

00:30:05.428 --> 00:30:07.597
...for the 12th straight year!
[Cheering]

00:30:07.597 --> 00:30:10.433
- I wish Super Bowl expectations were this low!

00:30:10.934 --> 00:30:12.060
- Could've been worse.

00:30:12.060 --> 00:30:13.061
- I love it here.

00:30:13.061 --> 00:30:14.687
- Look, look, watch.

00:30:14.687 --> 00:30:17.315
Du...falllll.

00:30:18.441 --> 00:30:20.944
- It's all good. I'm about to be Kirk Cousins rich.

00:30:21.736 --> 00:30:23.571
- Look, the kickers parade's starting.

00:30:23.571 --> 00:30:25.990
- [Crowd:] It's OK, we blame Dak!

00:30:25.990 --> 00:30:27.617
- Sorry we weren't here sooner.

00:30:27.617 --> 00:30:29.494
We accidentally beat the Bucs.

00:30:29.494 --> 00:30:31.955
- Is it really not all about winning?

00:30:31.955 --> 00:30:34.707
- Yo, we're trying to rest for the playoffs that we're still in.

00:30:34.707 --> 00:30:36.876
- Our...apologies...

00:30:37.836 --> 00:30:38.586
- Losing sucks!

00:30:38.586 --> 00:30:40.839
- Everyone, get them!

00:30:40.839 --> 00:30:42.715
- [All:] Aaaaaah!

00:30:47.095 --> 00:30:50.098
- So, uh...how...how's Davante?

00:30:50.098 --> 00:30:52.350
- Oh, you, uh, didn't hear? We broke up.

00:30:52.350 --> 00:30:54.769
- Oh, wow, that's...I'm sorry to hear that.

00:30:54.769 --> 00:30:57.856
- Yeah, well, think he never got over an old flame.

00:30:57.856 --> 00:30:59.065
Go to him, Aaron.
[Romantic music swells]

00:30:59.065 --> 00:30:59.482
- But-

00:30:59.482 --> 00:31:02.735
- I wouldn't be Derek Carr if I didn't love love.

00:31:02.735 --> 00:31:04.821
Now, go to him before it's too late.

00:31:09.075 --> 00:31:10.660
[Door opening]
- I know what the f--k I'm doing.

00:31:10.660 --> 00:31:11.786
I'm allowed to be here.

00:31:11.786 --> 00:31:13.663
- There's vomit on your sweater already?

00:31:13.663 --> 00:31:15.415
- Little Caesars hot and ready.

00:31:15.415 --> 00:31:18.042
- Stop rapping about vomit. We're up next.

00:31:18.042 --> 00:31:19.460
- ♪♪♪ Oh boy, looks like you've been slain

00:31:19.460 --> 00:31:22.797
by my No. 1 guy with a high ankle sprain! ♪♪♪

00:31:22.797 --> 00:31:24.424
- [Crowd:] Oooh!

00:31:24.424 --> 00:31:25.800
- [Together:] Good game. Good game.

00:31:25.800 --> 00:31:27.844
- There's nothing young white coaches love more than "8 Mile."

00:31:27.844 --> 00:31:30.096
- NFC, let's get ready for the final battle.

00:31:30.096 --> 00:31:32.432
- ♪♪♪ Lance, Jimmy G., gave the rock to Purdy.

00:31:32.432 --> 00:31:34.934
Mr. Irrelevant and Imma still hang 30. ♪♪♪

00:31:34.934 --> 00:31:35.435
- [Crowd:] Oooh!

00:31:35.435 --> 00:31:37.687
- ♪♪♪ You had four QBs, whoops now you've got none.

00:31:37.687 --> 00:31:40.023
Oh, what an offensive GENIUS, another Deebo run. ♪♪♪

00:31:40.023 --> 00:31:41.065
- [Crowd:] Oooh!

00:31:41.065 --> 00:31:43.526
- ♪♪♪ Got big dreams, and think you're getting closer.

00:31:43.526 --> 00:31:46.404
What's that? DPOY Nick Bosa. ♪♪♪

00:31:46.404 --> 00:31:47.447
- [Crowd:] Oooh!

00:31:47.447 --> 00:31:49.157
- You said Toby Keith was performing.

00:31:49.157 --> 00:31:51.409
- ♪♪♪ Hate to pan the man, but he's just a nepo baby.

00:31:51.409 --> 00:31:54.662
Hey Shanahan, how many snubs you get from Brady? ♪♪♪

00:31:54.662 --> 00:31:55.788
- [Crowd:] Oooh!

00:31:55.788 --> 00:31:56.915
- All right, playas.

00:31:56.915 --> 00:31:59.042
Winner is decided by whoever gets the loudest.

00:31:59.042 --> 00:32:00.084
- How does that make sense?

00:32:00.084 --> 00:32:02.170
- Aaaah. LOUD SCREAMING.

00:32:02.795 --> 00:32:04.964
- ♪♪♪ Nicky Sirianni says Nicky Sayonara.

00:32:04.964 --> 00:32:07.050
31-7 is the final score-a.

00:32:07.050 --> 00:32:10.595
Fly Eagles fly, bye Niners byeeee. ♪♪♪

00:32:10.595 --> 00:32:11.679
[Cheering]

00:32:11.679 --> 00:32:12.931
- Philly wins!
[Knocking]

00:32:12.931 --> 00:32:14.432
Oh, no, the stripes are here! Run!

00:32:14.432 --> 00:32:15.391
[Whistles]

00:32:19.771 --> 00:32:21.397
- Everybody else got dues to pay.

00:32:21.397 --> 00:32:23.191
Little Zac got a gig 'cause he met McVay.

00:32:23.191 --> 00:32:25.109
Hamburger eats, giant playsheets,

00:32:25.109 --> 00:32:27.528
Ya gonna get beat, I got Reid receipts!

00:32:27.528 --> 00:32:29.238
- Your weak-ass rhymes don't affect me.

00:32:29.238 --> 00:32:30.865
Could've been friends, you're my Bienemy.

00:32:30.865 --> 00:32:32.825
Joe Cool in the pocket making you pay,

00:32:32.825 --> 00:32:34.410
Got all the homies back in Cincy yellin':

00:32:34.410 --> 00:32:35.828
Oh, Who Dey?!

00:32:35.828 --> 00:32:37.288
- Take your time, we've got plenty of—

00:32:37.288 --> 00:32:38.539
[Explosion]

00:32:38.539 --> 00:32:39.332
- Nevermind, hurry up.

00:32:39.332 --> 00:32:42.168
- What's going on, Dad? I mean...Andy Reid.

00:32:42.168 --> 00:32:43.086
[Zombie attacking, growling]

00:32:43.086 --> 00:32:44.587
- No. Sweet baby Nick Foles.

00:32:45.421 --> 00:32:48.049
- I think a mutual change will benefit us both!

00:32:48.049 --> 00:32:50.301
- I agree! I'm leaving on good terms!

00:32:51.094 --> 00:32:52.679
- Yo, they say the kid is special.

00:32:53.346 --> 00:32:55.682
- Oh, wow. The world sure is interesting.

00:32:55.682 --> 00:32:57.100
What does this do?

00:32:57.100 --> 00:32:58.434
- Show him, Pat.

00:32:58.434 --> 00:33:00.061
- A high ankle sprain?

00:33:00.061 --> 00:33:01.562
But he's still moving.

00:33:01.562 --> 00:33:03.815
- I'm immune to bad things.

00:33:03.815 --> 00:33:05.650
- We need to take him to Arizona.

00:33:05.650 --> 00:33:06.818
- But it's been overrun...

00:33:06.818 --> 00:33:08.277
...by Philadelphians.

00:33:09.946 --> 00:33:11.823
- Go Birds.

00:33:11.823 --> 00:33:15.535
- Wow, another beautiful day in the zombie apocalypse.

00:33:15.535 --> 00:33:16.411
- [Together:] Oh, shocker.

00:33:16.411 --> 00:33:17.704
You're gonna make us the bad guys?

00:33:17.704 --> 00:33:19.789
Typical anti-Philly bias.

00:33:19.789 --> 00:33:22.291
- They're connected into one toxic hive mind.

00:33:22.291 --> 00:33:24.043
It's very scary.

00:33:24.043 --> 00:33:26.295
[Zombie growling]
[Clearing throat]

00:33:26.295 --> 00:33:27.714
- Sorry, I'm hometown hero Haason Reddick.

00:33:28.339 --> 00:33:29.298
[Glass cracking]

00:33:29.298 --> 00:33:30.842
- Scramble!
- Run! I'll block!

00:33:30.842 --> 00:33:31.718
- Do you still do that?

00:33:31.718 --> 00:33:32.468
- I'll try.

00:33:32.468 --> 00:33:34.804
- Aaaah! They sound so weird.

00:33:34.804 --> 00:33:36.723
- Woo! Jabroni thought he got me!

00:33:36.723 --> 00:33:39.475
- You've been infected...with Eaglemania.

00:33:39.475 --> 00:33:42.061
- No, no, I can stop this jawn! I mean...thing.

00:33:42.061 --> 00:33:44.313
- He's changing.

00:33:44.313 --> 00:33:46.649
[Zombie transformation sounds]

00:33:46.649 --> 00:33:49.944
- Hey, Jabronis...go Birds.

00:33:49.944 --> 00:33:52.530
- It's Eagle Kelce! Run!

00:33:52.530 --> 00:33:55.533
I think now might be a good time to give me some weapons.

00:33:56.576 --> 00:33:56.909
Here I am!

00:33:58.077 --> 00:33:58.661
Look, I slayed.

00:33:59.620 --> 00:34:00.288
- Aaah!

00:34:00.288 --> 00:34:02.248
- Illegal hurting of the main character.

00:34:02.248 --> 00:34:04.417
- I know it's not cool to say, but this kid is getting annoy—

00:34:05.084 --> 00:34:06.669
- This should be a fun level! I mean part.

00:34:07.295 --> 00:34:08.838
- Look, they've got runners...

00:34:08.838 --> 00:34:10.214
And All-Pro wideouts.

00:34:10.214 --> 00:34:12.216
- I thought those went extinct.

00:34:12.216 --> 00:34:13.301
[Thundering footsteps]

00:34:14.218 --> 00:34:15.970
- A Hurtser.

00:34:15.970 --> 00:34:18.097
- Even though I'm a zombie, I'm still very hot.

00:34:18.097 --> 00:34:20.308
- Every now and then, you do need some defense.

00:34:20.767 --> 00:34:23.478
- Chris Joooooones.

00:34:23.478 --> 00:34:24.812
- Damn right, I'm on fire.

00:34:24.812 --> 00:34:25.980
- Aaaah.

00:34:25.980 --> 00:34:28.566
- [Announcer:] Wow, two young guys making the most of a tough situation.

00:34:28.566 --> 00:34:30.443
Speaking of finding love in a hopeless place,

00:34:30.443 --> 00:34:33.029
stick around for "Fedra Presents: The Rihanna Half-Fight Show."

00:34:33.029 --> 00:34:35.907
- E, A, G, L...

00:34:35.907 --> 00:34:38.409
- M, N, O, P.

00:34:38.409 --> 00:34:39.202
- A battery?!

00:34:39.202 --> 00:34:40.203
- Time's up. Oh, wait...

00:34:40.203 --> 00:34:42.580
This watch is busted. Uh, time's yours.

00:34:45.541 --> 00:34:47.877
- Tyreek? Tyreek!

00:34:47.877 --> 00:34:50.922
If you find this, then I've gone to a better place.

00:34:50.922 --> 00:34:53.299
Or at least Miami...hehehe.

00:34:53.299 --> 00:34:54.675
I used to hate the world,

00:34:54.675 --> 00:34:55.593
But I was wrong.

00:34:55.593 --> 00:34:57.678
Because there was one person worth saving...

00:34:57.678 --> 00:34:58.429
Me!

00:34:59.097 --> 00:35:00.556
I wonder how I write him back!

00:35:00.556 --> 00:35:02.141
- I did it. I finally did it.

00:35:02.141 --> 00:35:04.393
Andrew Reid won a Super Bowl!!!

00:35:04.393 --> 00:35:05.895
- What a fun, easy sport.

00:35:05.895 --> 00:35:08.564
- I'm telling you all, this has happened before. Look.

00:35:08.564 --> 00:35:09.023
- [Phone speaker:] Andrew Reid won a Super—

00:35:09.023 --> 00:35:11.067
- OK, time for that darkness retreat.

00:35:11.067 --> 00:35:13.778
- We are stuck in a script of a show that just keeps repeating itself.

00:35:13.778 --> 00:35:15.154
And its name is—

00:35:18.074 --> 00:35:19.283
I wish I could see things clearly.

00:35:19.283 --> 00:35:21.285
- Try this. It's a little untraditional.

00:35:21.285 --> 00:35:21.911
- Say no more.

00:35:22.411 --> 00:35:25.665
Well, guess I'll go die on the Jets with my Wrangler jeans.

00:35:25.665 --> 00:35:27.667
Woah, some drink.

00:35:27.667 --> 00:35:29.794
- What's he smokin', huh?

00:35:29.794 --> 00:35:30.670
[Laugh track playing]

00:35:30.670 --> 00:35:33.005
- Expired Gatorade from when I was in St. Louis.

00:35:33.005 --> 00:35:34.173
[Laugh track playing]
- Back to work!

00:35:34.173 --> 00:35:36.300
JK, maybe this year I'll go back to work.

00:35:36.300 --> 00:35:37.552
[Awww]
- LOL!

00:35:37.552 --> 00:35:39.262
- Is it always like this?

00:35:39.262 --> 00:35:41.889
- B.O.B., will you be my O.C.?

00:35:41.889 --> 00:35:42.640
- Woah.

00:35:42.640 --> 00:35:44.559
- Can't wait to definitely play football this year.

00:35:44.559 --> 00:35:47.186
- Stefon Diggs is disgruntled.

00:35:47.186 --> 00:35:50.064
- Finally, one of my conspiracy theories is true.

00:35:50.064 --> 00:35:51.941
- Welcome, remember to dress up as your—

00:35:51.941 --> 00:35:54.652
- They're reusing scripts! We already did a whole Brady thing.

00:35:54.652 --> 00:35:55.570
- [Together:] Oh, yeah.

00:35:55.570 --> 00:35:56.654
- We're not trapped!

00:35:56.654 --> 00:35:58.156
Next year will be the Bills' year.

00:35:58.281 --> 00:35:59.448
- Next year will be the Bills' year.

00:35:59.949 --> 00:36:01.117
- Next year will be the Bills' year.

00:36:01.242 --> 00:36:02.410
Next year will be the Bills' year.

00:36:02.535 --> 00:36:03.703
Next year will be the Bills' year.

00:36:03.828 --> 00:36:04.996
Next year will be the Bills' year.

00:36:05.121 --> 00:36:06.831
- Oh, my gosh, he's right.

00:36:06.831 --> 00:36:08.207
Wait, where's Aaron?

00:36:08.207 --> 00:36:10.293
- People will come looking for me if I miss McAfee!

00:36:10.293 --> 00:36:11.544
Woah, a secret door.

00:36:11.544 --> 00:36:13.963
- Aaron, I'm so sorry I left you.

00:36:13.963 --> 00:36:16.174
- I know now...it wasn't your fault.

00:36:16.174 --> 00:36:17.675
[Paper printing]

00:36:17.675 --> 00:36:18.926
- It's next year's scripts.

00:36:18.926 --> 00:36:20.428
Saquon joins the Chiefs?

00:36:20.428 --> 00:36:21.804
OK, don't hate that one.

00:36:21.804 --> 00:36:23.931
- Hello, I am the Script Writer.

00:36:23.931 --> 00:36:26.726
I decide which storylines are epic enough to happen.

00:36:26.726 --> 00:36:28.853
- But free will! Why are you repeating everything?

00:36:28.853 --> 00:36:31.439
- OMG, spectacular catch, Davante.

00:36:31.439 --> 00:36:34.442
The thing is, people only want the same six scripts.

00:36:34.442 --> 00:36:36.319
Chiefs good. Refs bad.

00:36:36.319 --> 00:36:37.945
Chargers lost in a weird way.

00:36:37.945 --> 00:36:39.113
- [Together:] But we wanna win.

00:36:39.113 --> 00:36:40.740
- Then press the fire emoji.

00:36:40.740 --> 00:36:43.326
Destroy the next 100 years of football scripts.

00:36:43.326 --> 00:36:47.246
Choose chaos. That is, if you think that's what people really want.

00:36:47.246 --> 00:36:48.748
- F--k you, script writers.

00:36:48.748 --> 00:36:50.625
- Timeout! I like the routine.

00:36:50.625 --> 00:36:52.668
I underperform one year. I overperform the next.

00:36:52.668 --> 00:36:53.711
I get paid. Repeat.

00:36:53.711 --> 00:36:55.713
- But, Kirk, don't you wanna win?

00:36:55.713 --> 00:36:57.298
- I'm not sure I can.

00:36:57.298 --> 00:36:59.175
- Do you know why I'm so confident?

00:36:59.175 --> 00:37:00.801
- The cigar?
- Cuz you're really good at football?

00:37:00.801 --> 00:37:01.302
- Cuz you're super hot?

00:37:01.302 --> 00:37:03.095
- Because when the abyss stares at me,

00:37:03.095 --> 00:37:04.972
I stare it the f--k back.

00:37:04.972 --> 00:37:06.682
- Kirk, I believe a lot of wacky things.

00:37:06.682 --> 00:37:11.312
But I have to believe any of us, even you, could win.

00:37:11.687 --> 00:37:12.104
[Beeping]

00:37:12.104 --> 00:37:15.483
[Alarm sounding]
- Deleting scripts for Seasons 8-100.

00:37:15.483 --> 00:37:16.776
- [Josh Allen:] Wheeee!

00:37:23.658 --> 00:37:26.494
- Alright, time to approve next year's scripts.

00:37:27.662 --> 00:37:29.080
What? Where are the scripts?

00:37:29.080 --> 00:37:30.998
Davante and Aaron need to get back together,

00:37:30.998 --> 00:37:33.209
Clammy was supposed to come back in a big way.

00:37:33.209 --> 00:37:35.795
We were finally gonna do an Avengers Endgame parody.

00:37:35.795 --> 00:37:38.422
Every episode was gonna go so viral!

00:37:38.422 --> 00:37:40.675
No! The unknown!

00:37:40.675 --> 00:37:44.345
Anything can happen! Oh, god, what if the Lions are good?

00:37:44.845 --> 00:37:45.388
[Door creaking]
- Hello?

00:37:45.388 --> 00:37:46.180
Is someone there?

00:37:46.180 --> 00:37:47.431
- Uh, you're at a...

00:37:47.431 --> 00:37:49.225
darkness retreat?

00:37:49.225 --> 00:37:51.352
- What the hell is a darkness retreat?

00:37:51.352 --> 00:37:52.228
He'll never—
- Shh.

00:37:52.228 --> 00:37:53.980
- Ah, yes! A darkness retreat!

00:37:53.980 --> 00:37:56.691
And you must be my conscience.

00:37:56.691 --> 00:37:57.692
- ...Yes.

00:37:57.692 --> 00:37:59.026
I love player empowerment,

00:37:59.026 --> 00:38:00.820
but this season, Aaron got maybe

00:38:00.820 --> 00:38:02.113
TOO empowered.

00:38:02.154 --> 00:38:03.531
- So as punishment,

00:38:03.531 --> 00:38:04.865
we're brainwashing—no,

00:38:04.865 --> 00:38:06.659
strongly suggesting...

00:38:06.659 --> 00:38:08.369
that he join the Jets.

00:38:08.369 --> 00:38:09.203
No offense.

00:38:09.203 --> 00:38:10.997
- No offense is literally our problem.

00:38:10.997 --> 00:38:12.999
- Fine! I'm going to the Jets.

00:38:12.999 --> 00:38:14.542
So long as...

00:38:14.542 --> 00:38:16.877
- He wants us to sign the ghost of
Jordy Nelson,

00:38:16.877 --> 00:38:19.005
get McAfee hired at WFAN,

00:38:19.005 --> 00:38:20.589
gift him that Joe Namath jacket...

00:38:20.589 --> 00:38:22.967
- Much like my personal hero,
Scarlet Witch

00:38:22.967 --> 00:38:24.552
after she turns evil,

00:38:24.552 --> 00:38:26.887
I have eliminated all player autonomy

00:38:26.887 --> 00:38:27.513
and

00:38:27.513 --> 00:38:29.098
trapped them in a Gridiron Heights

00:38:29.098 --> 00:38:30.057
of my own making.

00:38:30.474 --> 00:38:31.100
I mean...

00:38:31.100 --> 00:38:31.809
we renovated.

00:38:34.603 --> 00:38:36.230
- [Producer:] Isn't that just the same Gridiron Heights

00:38:36.230 --> 00:38:37.231
but with a monorail?

00:38:37.315 --> 00:38:38.274
- What?! No!

00:38:38.274 --> 00:38:40.651
It's a new day in Gridiron Heights.

00:38:40.651 --> 00:38:41.819
We're restructuring

00:38:41.819 --> 00:38:43.112
with some old favorites

00:38:43.112 --> 00:38:44.613
in exciting new places.

00:38:45.239 --> 00:38:46.198
- Just win, baby.

00:38:46.198 --> 00:38:47.491
The tuck rule was a fumble.

00:38:47.491 --> 00:38:49.869
Josh McDaniels is a football genius.

00:38:49.869 --> 00:38:51.078
- Oh, and you're gonna love

00:38:51.078 --> 00:38:52.580
the direction we take Derek Carr

00:38:52.580 --> 00:38:54.081
in this season.

00:38:54.081 --> 00:38:56.125
- I'm fixin' to get me some etouffee

00:38:56.125 --> 00:38:57.626
down there by the Quarter, now.

00:38:57.626 --> 00:38:59.420
- Some players were easier to

00:38:59.420 --> 00:39:02.006
reprogram—I mean convince—than others!

00:39:02.006 --> 00:39:02.631
- Um, Jalen,

00:39:02.631 --> 00:39:03.716
some people were talking shit

00:39:03.716 --> 00:39:05.259
saying you'll never play for the Dolphins?

00:39:05.718 --> 00:39:06.844
- MAN! I'LL SHOW THEM.

00:39:06.844 --> 00:39:08.846
- Before long, we'll have the
Gridiron Heights

00:39:08.846 --> 00:39:10.056
I've always dreamed of,

00:39:10.056 --> 00:39:12.350
with exciting new characters!

00:39:26.155 --> 00:39:26.906
- Hmmm,

00:39:26.906 --> 00:39:28.282
I think I could mold you.

00:39:28.282 --> 00:39:30.534
- Some characters will have to be...

00:39:30.534 --> 00:39:31.285
retired.

00:39:31.285 --> 00:39:32.953
- Goodnight, Ezekiel.

00:39:32.953 --> 00:39:34.955
I loved you the very most.

00:39:34.955 --> 00:39:36.040
- But I didn't retire.

00:39:36.040 --> 00:39:37.124
You can just re-sign me!

00:39:37.375 --> 00:39:39.835
- I'm happy we got to an agreement.

00:39:39.835 --> 00:39:40.836
- Gridiron Heights:

00:39:40.836 --> 00:39:41.837
It's normal,

00:39:41.837 --> 00:39:43.631
good and free of scandal.

00:39:43.631 --> 00:39:45.758
- YOU CAN'T MAKE ME SELL!

00:39:45.758 --> 00:39:48.427
- TEAMY DISTANCING HIMSELF
FROM SNYDER!

00:39:48.427 --> 00:39:49.804
RAWR!!!
[Crashing]

00:39:50.638 --> 00:39:52.223
- This is your fault for not having an agent.

00:39:54.767 --> 00:39:56.685
- They said they're sending me to a team upstate

00:39:56.685 --> 00:39:58.771
where I'll have
plenty of room to scramble!

00:39:58.771 --> 00:40:01.649
- They'll be back for us any minute now.

00:40:01.649 --> 00:40:03.150
Annnnnny minute.

00:40:03.150 --> 00:40:04.402
- Baltimore's gonna come a-calling,

00:40:04.402 --> 00:40:05.361
just you wait.

00:40:05.820 --> 00:40:06.404
- Nexts years my year.

00:40:06.404 --> 00:40:06.987
- I could make a comeback.

00:40:06.987 --> 00:40:09.323
- Nexts years my year.
- I could make a comeback.

00:40:09.323 --> 00:40:11.242
- I'm Ryan Leaf. Get me out of here.

